<title>GERMANY: Springer says 96 net profit rises 15.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Springer says 96 net profit rises 15.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German media group Axel Springer Verlag AG said on Thursday 1996 group net profits rose 15.5 percent to 164 million marks ($97.1 million) on a 4.3 percent rise in turnover to 4.426 billion marks.</p>
<p>The company, which owns the mass circulation Bild newspaper and a stake in the cable channel SAT 1, also said it planned to raise its dividend to 20 marks per share from 17 marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150 ($ = 1.688 German Marks)</p>
